    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-8463",
      "problem": "Given $X \\sim U \\left\\lbrace 7, 8, 9, \\ldots, 16\\right\\rbrace,$ compute $P(8 \\leq          X < 13).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14268989/assets/830df36f7ea0a89f13fcb1f11f7f5b787fb9d099fd10b019ba0172168f279772.svg)\n\nHere, we have $X \\sim U \\left\\lbrace 7, 8, 9, \\ldots, 16 \\right\\rbrace,$ and the set $S = \\left\\lbrace 7, 8, 9, \\ldots, 16 \\right\\rbrace$ has $|S|=16 - 7 + 1 = 10$ items. So, we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14268989/assets/2002f51379a57bd014409bed9fb7c3153a6c8047305e51894371bd9d63b9b32b.svg)\n\nIn $S,$ there are $5$ items $(8, 9, 10, 11, 12)$ that satisfy $8 \\leq  X < 13.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(8 \\leq  X < 13) = 5 \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{10} = \\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$",
